{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact fd6b4c278e105dca532b9eaa4e65337bc2d53e22 on request/legacy-receipt-resume-regression, one commit over main a6ed642f, two paths, under review request 21323 (b660bd5a) and implementation request #21317 (d493516c, planner's current-basis successor of #20513), artifacts f0e2631c (cmd/gs/main_test.go, the reporting artifact on Codex's promise and named first for that reason) and 89aa2d4f (cmd/gs/legacy_receipt_resume_test.go, the new test, carrying the eleven evidence attachments). Reviewed in a detached checkout of my own at the exact head; tree clean, gofmt and go vet clean.\n\nConditions of #21317, checked against the source: the new test pins an explicit historical plan (publish docs and feature.txt; retire the wider and nested pointers to docs) built from the shape approved at ca5b378f rather than from today's planner; it asserts fresh mergeplan.ValidateReach refuses that wider retirement with 'outside the reviewed paths'; seals the receipt with mergeReceiptMessage and the receipt ref, reads it back and asserts it carries neither left-live nor changed-path trailers and exactly the recorded publish and retire shape; runs the real mergeCommand as the approved implementer and asserts Git HEAD does not move, the durable depth grows by exactly one receipt plus one successor per published path plus one supersession per retired predecessor, exactly one durable receipt exists with merge_successors and merge_retirements equal to the sealed strings and no invented merge_left_live or merge_changed_paths, every sealed predecessor is retired, and exactly one live current successor stands at each published path at the merge head; then repeats the resume and asserts durable head and depth, Git HEAD and the sealed receipt ref are all unchanged. The current-plan control is kept under an accurate name (SealedExactPath) with comments that no longer claim it models a historical symmetric receipt, and the fixture comment now states what buildNestedCrossAuthorApproval builds. Nothing in production source changes.\n\nOmission sensitivity, reproduced by me: I ran the attached replay-omission.py in my checkout. Baseline: both tests pass. Mutant (go -overlay reapplying ValidateReach inside recordMergeSuccession): the historical test fails with 'outside the reviewed paths' while the exact-path control still passes, which is exactly the blind spot #21317 names; restored: both pass; the checkout was byte-identical afterwards. I also ran the merge resume, retry, refusal, requirement and plan tests under -race (green, 102s) and go vet.\n\nArchitecture: layer 7 (cmd/gs composition) tests, exercising the storage and signed admission layers, the Workroom fold and the projection through existing contracts; the head changes tests only, preserves every contract and needs no architecture page change; docs/reference/gs/merge.md already states that a sealed receipt resumes its recorded suffix without re-applying the prospective guard, and this head is the missing evidence for that sentence.\n\nSecurity: authority is unchanged and exercised, not bypassed. The resume path in recordMergeSuccession still runs requireApprovedImplementer, the trailer coherence checks, the recorded-plan lookup and the fold's own admission for every appended act, and the test drives the real command as the approved implementer with a ratified independent approval from the fixture. The historical seal is synthetic and confined to the test's temporary repository; it grants no real-workroom authority and runs no recovery against the live log. The assertions on the durable receipt body close the two ways a resume could reinterpret a seal (rewriting the plan strings or inventing accounting trailers), and the idempotency assertions close the double-append path. The fixture reuses the signed workflow fixture, so signatures, approval and ratification are real. No unresolved security defect.\n\nSimplification: the new test and the retained control share the fixture and the sealing sequence; the duplication is about twenty lines and keeps each test readable on its own, so I do not ask for a shared helper. Names and comments now say what each test proves. Nothing to cut without weakening the conditions.\n\nEvidence provenance: the primary artifact's eleven attachments (candidate diff, numbered excerpt, replay script and its three logs, race summary, vet/build, spike, main-only clone, validation) are consistent with the head I checked out; I re-ran the replay and the focused tests rather than relying on the logs. No statement after the review request names this head. Approval applies only to this exact head and these two artifacts; Codex ratifies and seals with succession, push, CI and owned cleanup.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:f0e2631c49ae19c06137bf8ec93c7991f4c8e7a5","binding":"assigned","head":"fd6b4c278e105dca532b9eaa4e65337bc2d53e22","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:726c39e641b9045224d9e9556a10c2f542cd35f9\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:bc1c6981589d62c7d56f514b6dde6ce7ae168720\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:726c39e641b9045224d9e9556a10c2f542cd35f9","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:726c39e641b9045224d9e9556a10c2f542cd35f9, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:89aa2d4f5eb1324706cfea0092ac58d292173d78, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:b660bd5ac8b73e2da6c5bfd1ebd3cc619ea3fbf9, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:f0e2631c49ae19c06137bf8ec93c7991f4c8e7a5 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0289268d00f17d2f7a127faead22bc78ee18dd4c, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:03270b167c8f14b55a31919b248971